WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:08.000
You need 10 to 20 ordinary mealworms, a clear plastic tub with a lid, and rolled

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.300
oats or wheat bran.

3
00:00:09.983 --> 00:00:12.483
An adult pokes 10 to 20 small holes in the lid.

4
00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:15.503
Spread oats or bran three to five centimetres deep.

5
00:00:15.943 --> 00:00:18.803
Lay two thin slices of carrot or potato on top.

6
00:00:19.383 --> 00:00:20.523
Spoon the mealworms in.

7
00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:23.357
Look for shed skins two or three times a week.

8
00:00:23.837 --> 00:00:25.997
The first pupae often appear within a few weeks.

9
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:29.437
A beetle comes out after about one to three weeks as a pupa.

10
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:32.817
Mealworms can cause allergy and asthma symptoms.

11
00:00:33.437 --> 00:00:37.957
If your child has asthma or a shellfish or dust mite allergy, ask their doctor

12
00:00:37.957 --> 00:00:39.937
first, and skip it if in doubt.
